  "comment": "One part of the Chauvet DJ GigBAR MOVE + ILS, patched as its own fixture at the bar's start address plus the part's offset (docs/GIGBAR_RIG.md). The bar itself must be in its 52CH (Version 2) or 50CH DMX mode. CLASS 3R LASER: the manual requires 3 m between the floor and the lowest beam and 3 m from the audience. Not patched by default; never let the look engine drive it. 27 Nov 2026: the colour channel is described as a wheel (its seven diode combinations as colours a look can match, 0-5 as its closed slot) and the strobe as a shutter, so the lights' scenes, effects and transitions work the laser as any light; the rotation stays a function channel.",
